{"id":"alberta","name":"Fort McMurray boreal forest","country":"Canada","story":"Boreal crown fires, including the May 2016 Horse River fire and the 2023 record season.","places":["Fort McMurray","Alberta","Wood Buffalo"],"lang":["en","fr"],"bbox":[-113.5,55.5,-110.0,58.5],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-10","built_at":"2026-11-10T16:40:27+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean); intervals widened so 95% of held-out months fall inside (MODIS-denial test)","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it"},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[1.5502,1.5263,1.3802,1.2944,1.2603,1.1052,1.243,1.8443,1.3391,1.1942,1.4334,1.3484],"pooled":1.2227,"sigma2":0.0573,"tau2":0.0533,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918,0.1918],"pooled":0.1918,"sigma2":0.2959,"tau2":0.0,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.2251,0.9245,0.9565,0.9222,0.9705,1.1243,0.7814,0.9256,0.9816,0.964,0.8778,0.9504],"pooled":0.9794,"sigma2":0.0309,"tau2":0.0181,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073,1.1073],"pooled":1.1073,"sigma2":0.0094,"tau2":0.0,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.2061,0.1934,0.2326,0.1934,0.1512,0.2555,0.1524,0.2137,0.3756,0.1934,0.2479,0.2751],"